  "subject": "A 48-year-old clerk in a Sheung Wan shipping office fills in the morning paper's Sudoku in ball-pen before the pantry kettle boils, and the whole floor thinks he is a genius, though he just writes any numbers because nobody ever checks; when the tea lady spots three sevens in one row he confesses to everyone, and nobody believes him: so clever, they say, and modest too.",
  "caption": "Cantonese zydeco two-step, Louisiana dance-hall shuffle. Piano accordion pumping bluesy riffs and squeeze-box swells, steel rubboard scraped in steady sixteenths, clean electric guitar chanking the off-beats, bouncing electric bass two-step, drum kit with double-kick shuffle and stop-time breaks. Warm live dance-hall mix, accordion and rubboard forward. Male baritone, jovial and gritty-warm, punchy on-the-beat phrasing, clearly sung melody on every line. Clear full voice, every word enunciated, steady sung melody on every line. 116 BPM, C major. Jovial, cocky, self-mocking foot-stomper. No trap drums, no autotune, no rap, no synth pads, no EDM drops, no slow ballad sections.",
